<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Dec trade gap $228 mln vs $169 mln in Nov.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Dec trade gap $228 mln vs $169 mln in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	Dec 96	Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Exports mln USD	 168	   179	 n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		   396	   348	 n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		  -228	  -169	 n.a.</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE FIGURES Jan-Dec     Jan-Nov</p>
<p> Exports mln USD     1,842	 1,615	 n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		 4,102	 3,576	 n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		-2,260	-1,961	 n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Comparative figures for the previous year are not available as the country was under an international trade embargo that was lifted on October 1 after nearly four and a half years.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
